From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:12:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2713/2713] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on HP OmniBook 5
 16

The HP OmniBook 5 16 (bf1xxx, Snapdragon X2 Elite, Mahua) keeps its EFI
variables behind the UEFI secure application, as the other Snapdragon X
laptops do. Add it to the QSEECOM allowlist so that efivarfs and the
PMIC RTC's UEFI time offset work.

[Birk Skyum: rebased onto Linux 7.3, whose allowlist has
hp,omnibook-5 and hp,omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx around it]
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index c5242d1..745b082 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2322,6 +2322,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-ultra-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-x-g2q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-5" },
+	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-5-16-bf1xxx" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-x14" },
 	{ .compatible = "huawei,gaokun3" },
-- 
2.47.3

